Edit 10: Add copyonwrite_prepare after setupexport (before send_export_info). The upstream version uses dirname/basename. I decided to use g_path_get_dirname/g_path_get_basename to avoid modification bugs. Also, to make sure all pages that may be touched can be covered, I'll use ceiling division for the difmap allocation.

Wait, I need to be careful about ceiling division: upstream uses `calloc(client->exportsize/DIFFPAGESIZE, sizeof(uint32_t))` and initializes `for (i=0;i<client->exportsize/DIFFPAGESIZE;i++)`. If I use ceiling division, then for sizes that are aligned to the page boundary, the loop count stays the same. For unaligned sizes, the extra entry covers the trailing page. I'll write it like this:

```c
